! Silicon, 2 atoms in the primitive fcc cell, ultrasoft, PBE.
!
! si2-us.in with the PBE dataset in place of the LDA one: same cell, same cutoffs,
! same k-points, so the difference between the two references is the gradient
! correction and nothing else. It is the ultrasoft path's check that the
! correction is evaluated on the *dense* grid, where the augmentation charge
! lives, and therefore sees the augmented density rather than the smooth one.
!
! conv_thr is tightened far past what the answer needs so that both codes run to
! the same fixed point and the energy terms can be compared digit by digit.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=20.0, ecutrho=160.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS
  2
   0.250000  0.250000  0.250000   1.00
   0.250000  0.250000  0.750000   3.00
